  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(m+5)! & =(m+5)(m+4)! \\\\ 2m! & =2m(2m-1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(m+4)!$ and $(2m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2m)!\\,(m+4)!}{(m+5)!\\,(2m-1)!} & =\\frac{(2m)\\,\\cdot (2m-1)!\\cdot (m+4)!}{(m+5)\\cdot (m+4)!\\cdot (2m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2m)\\,\\cdot \\cancel{(2m-1)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(m+4)!}}{(m+5)\\cdot \\cancel{(m+4)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(2m-1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2m}{m+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
